From: ihexon <zzheasy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: rockchip: i2s: add the XFER register default

I2S_XFER is readable, writable and non-volatile but has no regcache
default. Runtime resume syncs REGCACHE_FLAT before the first stream has
written XFER, causing a read of an invalid zero-initialized cache entry.
The same can occur on the first read-modify-write of the start bits.

The RK3399 TRM V1.4, Part 1, section 22.4 (pages 705 and 714), specifies a
reset value of zero for I2S_XFER (0x001c): both transmit and receive are
stopped. Record that value explicitly. Keep the existing cache policy and
all other register defaults.

Signed-off-by: ihexon <zzheasy@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_i2s.c b/sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_i2s.c
--- a/sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_i2s.c
+++ b/sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_i2s.c
@@ -623,6 +623,7 @@ static const struct reg_default rockchip_i2s_reg_defaults[] = {
 	{0x08, 0x00071f1f},
 	{0x10, 0x001f0000},
 	{0x14, 0x01f00000},
+	{I2S_XFER, 0x00000000},
 };
 
 static const struct regmap_config rockchip_i2s_regmap_config = {
